# PadPal v2 Engineering Workflow

Full details live in `WORKFLOW.md` at the project root. Read it at the start of every session involving code changes or Jira work.

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- **DO NOT** write any code unless explicitly told to work on a specific Jira ticket
- **DO NOT** refactor, optimize, or fix anything outside the current ticket's scope
- **STOP after opening a PR** — wait for explicit greenlight before starting the next ticket
- 1 Jira ticket = 1 feature branch = multiple atomic commits

## Jira

- Project key: `SCRUM` (Atlassian board: PadPal)
- Ticket URL format: `https://hiyabwoldegebriel.atlassian.net/browse/SCRUM-XXX`
- **Active sprint (highest priority):** "PadPal V2 - Phase 0 Product Launch" (SCRUM-49+) — see `docs/product/plans/2026-06-08-design-system-rooms-roadmap.md`
- Phase 0 takes precedence over Phase 1–3 except SCRUM-1–3 (security)
- Reserved: SCRUM-63–67 (Capacitor)
- Phase 1 sprint: "PadPal V2 - Phase 1" (SCRUM-1 through SCRUM-18) — deferred unless blocking

## Branch Naming

```
feature/SCRUM-XXX-short-kebab-title
```

Cut all branches from `padpal-v2`.

## Commit Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description> [SCRUM-XXX]
```

Types: `feat` · `fix` · `perf` · `refactor` · `chore` · `docs`

## Design System v2 (SCRUM-74–86)

Before any Phase 0 design-system ticket (SCRUM-74–86), read `docs/design/v2-mockup-reference.md` and `src/design/README.md`. Update the mockup reference **decision log** when choices are locked during brainstorming or implementation. Delete `v2-mockup-reference.md` when SCRUM-79 + SCRUM-86 are merged.

## Execution Order Per Ticket

1. Read the Jira ticket and `AUDIT.md` reference
2. Read relevant source files before touching anything (design-system tickets: include `docs/design/v2-mockup-reference.md`)
3. Create feature branch off `padpal-v2`
4. Implement only the scoped change with atomic commits
5. Push branch and open PR using the mandatory template in `WORKFLOW.md`
6. Update Jira ticket to "In Review"
7. **STOP — wait for next instruction**

## Reference Files

| File | When to Read |
|------|-------------|
| `WORKFLOW.md` | Start of every session involving a ticket |
| `AUDIT.md` | Before implementing any fix — understand root cause |
| `docs/product/PRD.md` | Before implementing any feature — understand intended behavior |
| `docs/design/v2-mockup-reference.md` | Phase 0 design-system tickets (SCRUM-74–86) — mockup inventory + decision log; update incrementally |
| `src/design/README.md` | Phase 0 design-system tickets — token catalog |
